            ],
            [
              "E0505",
              "move while borrowed",
              "end the borrow first"
            ],
            [
              "E0507",
              "move out of borrow",
              "`clone`, `take`, own `self`"
            ],
            [
              "E0499",
              "two `&mut` at once",
              "split scopes, `split_at_mut`"
            ],
            [
              "E0502",
              "`&mut` while `&` alive",
              "classic `v.push(v[0])`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "E0106 missing lifetime specifier",
            "You returned a reference tied to no input"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Loops Eat Values"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "for _ in 0..3 {",
            "    consume(s); // E0382 on pass two",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Clone inside the loop, or move the loop",
            "`for x in v` then using `v` after — write `for x in &v`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Silent Ones"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let _ = mutex.lock().unwrap();",
            "// lock released instantly, section broken"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Nothing warns you; the code just races",
            "Bind `_guard` to hold it for the scope",
            "Struct fields drop in declaration order, not reverse"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Clone To Shut It Up",
          "text": "It compiles, and it hides an ownership design that wanted a `&` or a restructure. Sometimes right, never reflexive."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Checks Moved To Runtime"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Rc<RefCell<T>>` defers borrow checking to run time",
            "A second `borrow_mut()` panics instead of failing to build"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Pointers That Rot"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Returning a reference to a local — it dies at return",
            "Return the owned value instead",
            "Self-referential struct: a move invalidates the inner pointer",
            "Use indices, `Pin`, or an arena"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "borrow",
              "restructure",
              "mem::take",
              "clone",
              "Rc / Arc"
