    {
      "page_title": "Errors You Will Actually Hit (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Fix Ladder",
          "text": "Work left to right and stop at the first that works. Every step right costs more than the one before it."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What It Costs At Runtime",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Nothing: no GC pause, no refcount traffic, no tracing",
            "Every check is erased after compilation",
            "The bill is paid in compile time and learning effort"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Move Cost In Practice"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A move memcpy's the stack part only",
            "LLVM elides most of them entirely",
            "Returning a large `Vec` by value is cheap"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "fn make() -> BigStruct {",
            "    BigStruct::new() // built in caller's slot",
            "} // return value optimization, no copy"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Operation",
            "Cost"
