    {
      "page_title": "Trade-offs and Design",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Pick The Owner",
          "text": "Make the owner the thing with the longest, clearest lifetime. Everything else borrows from it."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Whole Model, Six Words",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "One owner, one drop, at scope exit",
          "text": "Non-Copy assignment moves and kills the source. Copy assignment duplicates it and keeps both alive."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Copy Set"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Integers, floats, `bool`, `char`, `&T`",
            "Tuples and arrays of Copy types",
            "Nothing that owns heap memory",
            "`Drop` and `Copy` never on the same type"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Why Copy And Drop Clash"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A Copy duplicate would run drop twice",
            "Compiler rejects both traits: E0184",
            "Copy is semantics, not size",
            "`[u8; 4096]` is Copy; `String` at 24 bytes is not"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Order Card"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Thing",
            "Drops in"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "locals",
              "reverse declaration"
            ],
            [
              "struct fields",
              "declaration order"
            ],
            [
              "tuple, array items",
              "index order"
            ],
            [
              "temporaries",
              "end of statement"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`drop(x)` forces an early release, anywhere"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worked Example: Drop Order"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let a = G(\"a\");",
            "let b = G(\"b\");",
            "// prints: dropping b, then dropping a"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Reverse because later bindings may borrow earlier ones",
            "A bare `{ }` block releases a guard early",
            "Shadowing does not drop the shadowed value early",
            "A moved value drops at the new owner's scope end"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
